      "basis": "VDR-CSO-DAC states no timeframe, so a window here is only the provider's own detectBy, and a change without a window is tracked but never lapses. Changes are measured against the provider-supplied inventory named by its SHA-256 digest, so a resource it omits is listed as unregistered and opens no obligation. A detection obligation is satisfied only by a verification at or after the change and at or before as-of; an examination that verified nothing does not satisfy one, and neither does untimed evidence. A created change and a new entry's coverage clocks overlap on purpose, under different rules. A detected status is not a compliance finding.",
